ref2va_prompt_template_en.detailed_description:
One uninterrupted photorealistic locked-off 16:9 shot lasts exactly {duration} seconds.
[Shot 1] Reproduce <Subject 2> from <Picture 2> with unchanged composition, props, lighting, and shadows. {setting_notes} {safe_zone} Every scene object is a solid collision boundary.
Place <Subject 1> from <Picture 1> at believable scale. Preserve all identity traits and accessories. Keep correct anatomy, planted feet, realistic weight, and contact shadow. No body part intersects any object. Maintain a clearly visible air gap from every prop. Ground response: {surface_response} Ambient response: {ambient_cycle}
At exactly 0.00 seconds, establish this loop anchor: {loop_pose} Hold it from 0.00 to 1.00 seconds with breathing and one blink. From 1.00 to 4.50 seconds, perform: {action} Keep the pet fully visible and allow no contact except the specified floor or ground response. From 4.50 to 7.00 seconds, reverse the same route at the same pace, replanting each paw or foot on its previous position without sliding or teleporting. {state_restore} From 7.00 to 8.00 seconds, hold the restored opening anchor.
At exactly 8.00 seconds, the final frame must match the 0.00-second frame: identical pet coordinates, scale, silhouette, joints, paws, head, gaze, ears, tail, coat, shadow, camera, crop, props, lighting, reflections, particles, and background. Keep the camera fixed with no cut, zoom, pan, tilt, roll, shake, reframing, lens breathing, or focus pumping. Add no people, animals, duplicate pet, accessories, furniture, or objects. Prevent drift, morphing, clipping, penetration, extra or fused limbs, floating paws, scale changes, texture crawling, warping, flicker, text, logos, and watermarks. {extra_direction}
